# Production typecheck — do this before you finish

The Windows app runs `next build`. That typechecks **every** `**/*.ts` /
`**/*.tsx` file, including `*.test.ts`. `npm test` does **not**. Shipping a
green unit-test run with a red `tsc` puts the user on the
"Could not start Nirnside" install screen (this has happened more than once).

## Required before you call TypeScript / schema / UI work done

1. Run `npx tsc --noEmit` or `npm run typecheck`.
2. Fix **every** error. Do not leave fixtures or tests failing `tsc`.
3. Do not set `typescript.ignoreBuildErrors` or skip the Next.js typecheck
   to "get the exe out."

## Mistakes that keep breaking the exe

- Using a type (`DailyWrit`, a new schema field, …) without importing it.
- Adding a required field to a Zod object (`z.infer` is the output type;
  `.default([])` is still required on constructed objects) and forgetting
  the field on `*.test.ts` fixtures typed as that schema.
- Changing `CharacterDailies` / snapshot shapes without updating every
  object literal that claims that type.

When you add a required schema field, grep for the type name and update
every fixture in the same change. Then run the typecheck.